### 2.2 Schema Stacking Best Practices

#### Multi-Schema Pages
For pages that warrant multiple schema types, stack them using an array:

```typescript
<>
  <JsonLd type="LocalBusiness" data={localBusinessData} />
  <JsonLd type="FAQPage" data={faqData} />
  <JsonLd type="WebSite" data={websiteData} />
</>
```

#### Website Schema (Layout Level)
```typescript
<JsonLd
  type="WebSite"
  data={{
    name: "Sun Gulf Realty",
    url: "https://sungulfrealty.com",
    potentialAction: {
      "@type": "SearchAction",
      target: "https://sungulfrealty.com/search?q={search_term_string}",
      "query-input": "required name=search_term_string"
    },
    publisher: {
      "@type": "Organization",
      name: "Sun Gulf Realty, LLC"
    }
  }}
/>
```

## 3. Title Tag Optimization Rules

### 3.1 Title Structure Patterns
- **Homepage**: `[Brand] - [Primary Service] [Location] | [Differentiator]`
- **Property**: `[Address] | [Beds]BR/[Baths]BA | $[Price] | [Location]`
- **Neighborhood**: `[Neighborhood] [Location] Real Estate | Homes for Sale | [Brand]`
- **Service**: `[Service] in [Location] | [Brand] | [Benefit/Differentiator]`
- **Blog**: `[Post Title] | [Brand] Blog`

### 3.2 Title Optimization Rules
- Keep titles 50-60 characters maximum
- Include primary keyword within first 30 characters
- Always include location (Cape Coral, Fort Myers, etc.)
- Use pipe (|) separators for better readability
- Include price for property listings
- Avoid keyword stuffing

## 4. Meta Description Rules

### 4.1 Description Patterns
- **Length**: 150-160 characters maximum
- **Include**: Primary keyword, location, call-to-action
- **Tone**: Benefit-driven, action-oriented
- **Format**: Problem/solution or benefit statement + CTA

### 4.2 Description Templates
```typescript
// Property listing
`${bedrooms} bedroom, ${bathrooms} bathroom ${propertyType} in ${neighborhood}, Cape Coral. ${topFeatures}. Contact Sun Gulf Realty for a showing today.`

// Neighborhood page  
`Discover ${neighborhood} Cape Coral real estate. Browse homes for sale, neighborhood insights, and market trends. Your local experts at Sun Gulf Realty.`

// Service page
`Expert ${service} in Cape Coral and Southwest Florida. Transparent, detail-oriented approach. Get your free consultation with Sun Gulf Realty today.`
```

## 5. Image Optimization for SEO

### 5.1 Alt Text Rules
- **Property images**: `"[PropertyType] at [Address], Cape Coral - [Key Feature]"`
- **Team photos**: `"[Name], Real Estate Agent at Sun Gulf Realty"`
- **Neighborhood**: `"[Neighborhood] Cape Coral - [Notable Feature]"`
- **Logo**: `"Sun Gulf Realty - Cape Coral Real Estate Agent"`

### 5.2 File Naming Convention
- Use descriptive, keyword-rich filenames
- Include location when relevant
- Use hyphens (not underscores)
- Examples: `cape-coral-waterfront-home-for-sale.jpg`, `sun-gulf-realty-team-photo.jpg`

## 6. Local SEO Optimization

### 6.1 NAP Consistency
Ensure Name, Address, Phone consistency across:
- Website footer
- Contact page
- Schema markup
- Google Business Profile
- All citations

### 6.2 Location-Specific Content
- Create neighborhood landing pages for major Cape Coral areas
- Include local landmarks and amenities in descriptions
- Reference local schools, shopping, and recreation
- Use local terminology and neighborhood names

## 7. Technical SEO Requirements

### 7.1 Core Web Vitals
- Largest Contentful Paint (LCP): < 2.5s
- First Input Delay (FID): < 100ms  
- Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS): < 0.1

### 7.2 Mobile Optimization
- Use responsive design for all pages
- Optimize images with `next/image`
- Implement touch-friendly navigation
- Test on multiple device sizes

### 7.3 Page Speed Optimization
- Implement lazy loading for images
- Minimize JavaScript bundles
- Use CDN for image delivery
- Optimize font loading

## 8. Content Guidelines

### 8.1 Keyword Density
- Primary keyword: 1-3% density
- Secondary keywords: 0.5-1% density
- Natural language integration
- Avoid keyword stuffing

### 8.2 Content Structure
- Use H1 for main page title (include primary keyword)
- Use H2-H6 for logical content hierarchy
- Include local keywords in subheadings
- Use bullet points and numbered lists
- Implement table of contents for long pages

